en&#8217;s Assertiveness under Conditions of Prolonged Psycho-Emotional Stress&#8221;. The plan describes how research data will be collected, documented, stored, protected, anonymized, analyzed and shared in accordance with ethical principles.&#10;<div>&#10;</div><div>The study will involve questionnaire and psychodiagnostic data related to women&#8217;s assertiveness, psycho-emotional tension, self-regulation, resilience and psychological well-being. Since the research concerns psychological characteristics, all primary data will be anonymized and stored securely. Only anonymized and aggregated results may be shared in an open repository such as OSF.</div>","dmp_id":{"identifier":"b115f64a-5b72-42fa-8e37-eabe5153381e","type":"other"},"ethical_issues_exist":"unknown","language":"ukr","modified":"2026-05-08T07:53:02.828994Z","project":[{"description":"The research is conducted as part of the applicant’s dissertation project and is not supported by a separate external research grant.","funding":[{"funder_id":{"identifier":"self funded","type":"fundref"},"grant_id":{"identifier":"not-applicable ","type":"other"}}],"title":"No external grant funding"}],"title":"Data Management Plan: Assertiveness of Women under Prolonged Psycho-Emotional Stress"}}